## Commercial Purposes

A commercial purpose is a purpose intended to obtain commercial
advantage or monetary compensation. Examples include selling or
licensing the software for a fee, charging for access to it, offering
it as part of a paid hosted service, integrating it into a commercial
product or service, and using it to operate a for-profit tutoring,
training, or other business activity, except for the limited ordinary
teaching permission below.

These are not permitted purposes. Providing a free copy or free access
does not make a use noncommercial when the use is part of such an
activity. An organization's status or name alone does not create an
exception. Commercial use requires a separate written authorization
from the relevant copyright holder.

## Limited Ordinary Teaching Permission

A teacher or educational institution may use the software solely to
prepare lessons and teaching materials and to deliver ordinary classes
to its own students, including classes for which the teacher receives
a salary or the students pay tuition. This is a permitted purpose even
when the institution is for-profit.

This exception does not permit selling or renting the software,
charging for access to the software, selling it as a stand-alone paid
preparation or generation service, operating a paid software platform,
or integrating the software into another commercial product or service. It creates no rights in materials owned by third parties.

